<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33889" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Părĭum</span></b> , or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> , ĭi,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πάριον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Mysia</i>,
				<i>on the Propontis</i>, now <i>Kamares</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. H. Fragm. 4, 61, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1,
			19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 32, 40, § 141</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 2,
				622</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Părĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Parium</i>, <i>Parian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 13, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colonia,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Parium</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 11, 18, § 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colias,</span>”
				<i>a kind of fish</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					32, 11, 53, § 146</span></i>
			 (better read. Partianus).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
